-- Regulation W, 12 CFR 223.42: exemptions from the quantitative limits, the collateral requirements and the
-- low-quality asset prohibition.
--
-- Target compiler: main (see NOTES.md).
-- Each exemption is a predicate on facts stated to it: whether the conditions of the text are met.
-- A determination, approval or notice is a stated fact, and so is whether a period the text bounds by date, as
-- the Board may have extended it, is running.  What an exemption leaves in force is in regwb-effects.l4.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `regwb-nouns`
IMPORT `regwb-collateral`

§ `223.42(a) and (b): deposits and uncollected items`

-- (a): "Making a deposit in an affiliated depository institution ... or affiliated foreign bank that represents an
-- ongoing, working balance maintained in the ordinary course of correspondent business."
GIVEN
    inAnAffiliatedInstitutionOrForeignBank IS A BOOLEAN
    ongoingWorkingBalanceInTheOrdinaryCourse IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(a)
`exempt as a correspondent banking deposit` MEANS inAnAffiliatedInstitutionOrForeignBank AND ongoingWorkingBalanceInTheOrdinaryCourse

-- (b): "Giving immediate credit to an affiliate for uncollected items received in the ordinary course of business."
GIVEN
    immediateCreditToAnAffiliate  IS A BOOLEAN
    forUncollectedItemsInTheOrdinaryCourse IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(b)
`exempt as credit for uncollected items` MEANS immediateCreditToAnAffiliate AND forUncollectedItemsInTheOrdinaryCourse

§ `223.42(c): transactions secured by cash or U.S. government securities`

-- (c)(1): "Engaging in a credit transaction with an affiliate to the extent that the transaction is and remains secured
-- by: (i) Obligations of the United States or its agencies; (ii) Obligations fully guaranteed by the United States or
-- its agencies as to principal and interest; or (iii) A segregated, earmarked deposit account with the member bank".
GIVEN c IS A Collateral
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(c)(1)
`is cash or government collateral` MEANS
       c's `kind` EQUALS `Obligations of the United States or its agencies`
    OR c's `kind` EQUALS `Obligations fully guaranteed by the United States or its agencies as to principal and interest`
    OR c's `kind` EQUALS `A segregated, earmarked deposit account with the member bank for the sole purpose of securing credit transactions with affiliates`

-- The part of the transaction that is exempt: "to the extent that" it is secured, no more than the transaction itself.
GIVEN
    value IS A NUMBER
    cs    IS A LIST OF Collateral
GIVETH A NUMBER
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(c)
`exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` MEANS
    min value (sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD `effective value of collateral` c) (filter (GIVEN c YIELD `is cash or government collateral` c) cs)))

-- (c)(2) example: "A member bank makes a $100 non-amortizing term loan to an affiliate secured by U.S. Treasury securities
-- with a market value of $50 and real estate with a market value of $75. The value of the covered transaction is $50.
-- If the market value of the U.S. Treasury securities falls to $45 during the life of the loan, the value of the covered
-- transaction would increase to $55."
GIVEN
    value IS A NUMBER
    cs    IS A LIST OF Collateral
GIVETH A NUMBER
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(c)(2)
`value of a credit transaction after the exemption for cash or government securities` MEANS
    value MINUS `exempt part of a credit transaction secured by cash or government securities` value cs

§ `223.42(d) and (e): servicing affiliates and liquid assets`

-- (d): "Purchasing a security issued by any company engaged solely in providing services described in section 4(c)(1) of
-- the Bank Holding Company Act".
GIVEN
    purchaseOfASecurity IS A BOOLEAN
    issuerEngagedSolelyInServicesDescribedInSection4c1 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(d)
`exempt as a purchase of securities of a servicing affiliate` MEANS purchaseOfASecurity AND issuerEngagedSolelyInServicesDescribedInSection4c1

-- (e): "Purchasing an asset having a readily identifiable and publicly available market quotation and purchased at or
-- below the asset's current market quotation.  An asset has a readily identifiable and publicly available market quotation
-- if the asset's price is quoted routinely in a widely disseminated publication that is readily available to the general public."
GIVEN
    quotedRoutinelyInAWidelyDisseminatedPublication IS A BOOLEAN
    pricePaid                                       IS A NUMBER
    currentMarketQuotation                          IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(e)
`exempt as a purchase of a liquid asset` MEANS quotedRoutinelyInAWidelyDisseminatedPublication AND pricePaid AT MOST currentMarketQuotation

§ `223.42(f) and (g): securities bought from a securities affiliate`

-- (f): "Purchasing a security from a securities affiliate, if: (1) The security has a 'ready market,' as defined in 17 CFR
-- 240.15c3-1(c)(11)(i); (2) The security is eligible for a State member bank to purchase directly, ... and the member bank
-- records the transaction as a purchase of a security for purposes of its Call Report ...; (3) The security is not a
-- low-quality asset; (4) The member bank does not purchase the security during an underwriting, or within 30 days of an
-- underwriting, if an affiliate is an underwriter of the security, unless the security is purchased as part of an issue of
-- obligations of, or obligations fully guaranteed ... by, the United States or its agencies; (5) The security's price is
-- quoted routinely on an unaffiliated electronic service ..., provided that: (i) The price paid ... is at or below the
-- current market quotation ...; and (ii) The size of the transaction ... does not cast material doubt on the
-- appropriateness of relying on the current market quotation ...; and (6) The member bank maintains, for a period of two
-- years, records and supporting information ...".
GIVEN
    fromASecuritiesAffiliate    IS A BOOLEAN
    hasAReadyMarket             IS A BOOLEAN
    eligibleAndRecordedAsASecurity IS A BOOLEAN
    notALowQualityAsset         IS A BOOLEAN
    anAffiliateIsAnUnderwriter  IS A BOOLEAN
    boughtDuringOrWithin30DaysOfTheUnderwriting IS A BOOLEAN
    partOfAnIssueOfUnitedStatesObligations IS A BOOLEAN
    quotedOnAnUnaffiliatedElectronicService IS A BOOLEAN
    pricePaid                   IS A NUMBER
    currentMarketQuotation      IS A NUMBER
    sizeDoesNotCastMaterialDoubt IS A BOOLEAN
    recordsKeptForTwoYears      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(f)
`exempt as a purchase of a marketable security` MEANS
        fromASecuritiesAffiliate
    AND hasAReadyMarket
    AND eligibleAndRecordedAsASecurity
    AND notALowQualityAsset
    AND (NOT (anAffiliateIsAnUnderwriter AND boughtDuringOrWithin30DaysOfTheUnderwriting AND (NOT partOfAnIssueOfUnitedStatesObligations)))
    AND quotedOnAnUnaffiliatedElectronicService
    AND pricePaid AT MOST currentMarketQuotation
    AND sizeDoesNotCastMaterialDoubt
    AND recordsKeptForTwoYears

-- (g): "Purchasing a municipal security from a securities affiliate if: (1) The security is rated by a nationally recognized
-- statistical rating organization or is part of an issue of securities that does not exceed $25 million; (2) The security is
-- eligible for purchase by a State member bank ... and the member bank records the transaction as a purchase of a security ...;
-- and (3)(i) The security's price is quoted routinely on an unaffiliated electronic service ..., provided that: (A) The price
-- paid ... is at or below the current market quotation ...; and (B) The size of the transaction ... does not cast material
-- doubt ...; or (ii) The price paid for the security can be verified by reference to two or more actual, current price quotes
-- from unaffiliated broker-dealers ..., where: (A) The price quotes ... are based on a transaction similar in size ...; and
-- (B) The price paid is no higher than the average of the price quotes; or (iii) The price paid ... can be verified by
-- reference to the written summary provided by the syndicate manager ..., if the member bank: (A) Purchases the municipal
-- security during the underwriting period at a price that is at or below that indicated in the summary; and (B) Obtains a
-- copy of the summary from its securities affiliate and retains the summary for three years."
GIVEN
    fromASecuritiesAffiliate        IS A BOOLEAN
    ratedByARecognizedAgency        IS A BOOLEAN
    sizeOfTheIssue                  IS A NUMBER
    eligibleAndRecordedAsASecurity  IS A BOOLEAN
    quotedOnAnUnaffiliatedElectronicService IS A BOOLEAN
    pricePaid                       IS A NUMBER
    currentMarketQuotation          IS A NUMBER
    sizeDoesNotCastMaterialDoubt    IS A BOOLEAN
    twoOrMoreQuotesFromUnaffiliatedBrokerDealers IS A BOOLEAN
    quotesBasedOnASimilarSize       IS A BOOLEAN
    averageOfTheQuotes              IS A NUMBER
    boughtDuringTheUnderwritingAtOrBelowTheSummaryPrice IS A BOOLEAN
    copyOfTheSummaryObtainedAndKeptThreeYears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(g)
`exempt as a purchase of a municipal security` MEANS
        fromASecuritiesAffiliate
    AND (ratedByARecognizedAgency OR sizeOfTheIssue AT MOST 25000000)
    AND eligibleAndRecordedAsASecurity
    AND (    (quotedOnAnUnaffiliatedElectronicService AND pricePaid AT MOST currentMarketQuotation AND sizeDoesNotCastMaterialDoubt)
          OR (twoOrMoreQuotesFromUnaffiliatedBrokerDealers AND quotesBasedOnASimilarSize AND pricePaid AT MOST averageOfTheQuotes)
          OR (boughtDuringTheUnderwritingAtOrBelowTheSummaryPrice AND copyOfTheSummaryObtainedAndKeptThreeYears))

§ `223.42(h) to (k): repurchase agreements, new banks, bank mergers, loan purchases`

-- (h): "Purchasing from an affiliate an extension of credit that was originated by the member bank and sold to the affiliate
-- subject to a repurchase agreement or with recourse."
GIVEN
    purchaseFromAnAffiliate IS A BOOLEAN
    originatedByTheMemberBank IS A BOOLEAN
    soldSubjectToRepurchaseOrWithRecourse IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(h)
`exempt as a purchase subject to a repurchase agreement` MEANS purchaseFromAnAffiliate AND originatedByTheMemberBank AND soldSubjectToRepurchaseOrWithRecourse

-- (i): "The purchase of an asset from an affiliate by a newly formed member bank, if the appropriate Federal banking agency for
-- the member bank has approved the asset purchase in writing in connection with its review of the formation of the member bank."
GIVEN
    byANewlyFormedMemberBank IS A BOOLEAN
    approvedInWritingOnReviewOfTheFormation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(i)
`exempt as an asset purchase by a newly formed member bank` MEANS byANewlyFormedMemberBank AND approvedInWritingOnReviewOfTheFormation

-- (j): "Any merger or consolidation between a member bank and an affiliated depository institution or U.S. branch or agency of
-- a foreign bank, or any acquisition of assets or assumption of deposit liabilities by a member bank from an affiliated
-- depository institution or U.S. branch or agency of a foreign bank, if the transaction has been approved by the responsible
-- Federal banking agency pursuant to the Bank Merger Act".
GIVEN
    mergerOrAcquisitionWithAnAffiliatedInstitutionOrBranch IS A BOOLEAN
    approvedUnderTheBankMergerAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(j)
`exempt as a transaction approved under the Bank Merger Act` MEANS mergerOrAcquisitionWithAnAffiliatedInstitutionOrBranch AND approvedUnderTheBankMergerAct

-- (k): "Purchasing from an affiliate, on a nonrecourse basis, an extension of credit, if: (1) The extension of credit was
-- originated by the affiliate; (2) The member bank makes an independent evaluation of the creditworthiness of the borrower before
-- the affiliate makes or commits to make the extension of credit; (3) The member bank commits to purchase the extension of credit
-- before the affiliate makes or commits to make the extension of credit; (4) The member bank does not make a blanket advance
-- commitment to purchase extensions of credit from the affiliate; and (5) The dollar amount of the extension of credit, when
-- aggregated with the dollar amount of all other extensions of credit purchased from the affiliate during the preceding 12 calendar
-- months by the member bank and its depository institution affiliates, does not represent more than 50 percent (or such lower
-- percent as is imposed by the member bank's appropriate Federal banking agency) of the dollar amount of extensions of credit
-- originated by the affiliate during the preceding 12 calendar months."
-- `percentAllowed` is 50, or the lower percentage the agency has imposed.
GIVEN
    nonrecourse                 IS A BOOLEAN
    originatedByTheAffiliate    IS A BOOLEAN
    independentEvaluationBeforehand IS A BOOLEAN
    committedBeforehand         IS A BOOLEAN
    noBlanketAdvanceCommitment  IS A BOOLEAN
    thisAmount                  IS A NUMBER
    otherPurchasesInThePrecedingYear IS A NUMBER
    originatedInThePrecedingYear IS A NUMBER
    percentAllowed              IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(k)
`exempt as a nonrecourse purchase of an extension of credit` MEANS
        nonrecourse
    AND originatedByTheAffiliate
    AND independentEvaluationBeforehand
    AND committedBeforehand
    AND noBlanketAdvanceCommitment
    AND (thisAmount PLUS otherPurchasesInThePrecedingYear) TIMES 100 AT MOST originatedInThePrecedingYear TIMES percentAllowed
    AND percentAllowed AT MOST 50

§ `223.42(l): intraday extensions of credit`

-- (l)(1): "An intraday extension of credit to an affiliate, if the member bank: (i) Has established and maintains policies and
-- procedures reasonably designed to manage the credit exposure arising from the member bank's intraday extensions of credit to
-- affiliates in a safe and sound manner, including policies and procedures for: (A) Monitoring and controlling the credit exposure
-- ... to each affiliate and all affiliates in the aggregate; and (B) Ensuring that any intraday extension of credit ... complies
-- with the market terms requirement of § 223.51; (ii) Has no reason to believe that the affiliate will have difficulty repaying
-- the extension of credit in accordance with its terms; and (iii) Ceases to treat any such extension of credit ... as an intraday
-- extension of credit at the end of the member bank's business day in the United States."
-- (l)(2): an intraday extension of credit is one "that the member bank expects to be repaid, sold, or terminated, or to qualify for
-- a complete exemption under this regulation, by the end of its business day in the United States."
GIVEN
    expectedToEndByTheEndOfTheBusinessDay IS A BOOLEAN
    policiesAndProceduresMonitorExposure IS A BOOLEAN
    policiesAndProceduresEnsureMarketTerms IS A BOOLEAN
    noReasonToBelieveRepaymentWillBeDifficult IS A BOOLEAN
    ceasesToTreatItAsIntradayAtTheEndOfTheDay IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(l)
`exempt as an intraday extension of credit` MEANS
        expectedToEndByTheEndOfTheBusinessDay
    AND policiesAndProceduresMonitorExposure
    AND policiesAndProceduresEnsureMarketTerms
    AND noReasonToBelieveRepaymentWillBeDifficult
    AND ceasesToTreatItAsIntradayAtTheEndOfTheDay

§ `223.42(m) to (o): riskless principal, securities financing and commercial paper`

-- (m): "Purchasing a security from a securities affiliate of the member bank if: (1) The member bank or the securities affiliate
-- is acting exclusively as a riskless principal in the transaction; and (2) The security purchased is not issued, underwritten,
-- or sold as principal (other than as riskless principal) by any affiliate of the member bank."
GIVEN
    fromASecuritiesAffiliate IS A BOOLEAN
    actingExclusivelyAsARisklessPrincipal IS A BOOLEAN
    notIssuedUnderwrittenOrSoldAsPrincipalByAnAffiliate IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(m)
`exempt as a riskless principal purchase` MEANS
    fromASecuritiesAffiliate AND actingExclusivelyAsARisklessPrincipal AND notIssuedUnderwrittenOrSoldAsPrincipalByAnAffiliate

-- (n): "From September 15, 2008, until October 30, 2009 (unless further extended by the Board), securities financing transactions
-- with an affiliate, if: (i) The security or other asset financed ... is of a type that the affiliate financed in the U.S. tri-party
-- repurchase agreement market at any time during the week of September 8-12, 2008; (ii) The transaction is marked to market
-- daily and subject to daily margin-maintenance requirements, and the member bank is at least as over-collateralized ... as the
-- affiliate's clearing bank was ...; (iii) The aggregate risk profile ... is no greater than ...; (iv) The member bank's top-tier
-- holding company guarantees the obligations of the affiliate ... (or provides other security ... acceptable to the Board); and
-- (v) The member bank has not been specifically informed by the Board ... that the member bank may not use this exemption."
-- (n)(2)(i): a securities financing transaction is "(A) A purchase ... from an affiliate of a security or other asset, subject to
-- an agreement by the affiliate to repurchase ...; (B) A borrowing of a security by a member bank from an affiliate on a
-- collateralized basis; or (C) A secured extension of credit by a member bank to an affiliate."
-- Whether the period (as extended by the Board) is running is stated.
GIVEN
    periodIsRunning             IS A BOOLEAN
    isASecuritiesFinancingTransaction IS A BOOLEAN
    ofATypeFinancedInTheTriPartyMarketInThatWeek IS A BOOLEAN
    markedToMarketDailyAndAtLeastAsOverCollateralized IS A BOOLEAN
    aggregateRiskProfileNoGreater IS A BOOLEAN
    topTierHoldingCompanyGuarantees IS A BOOLEAN
    notInformedByTheBoardItMayNotUseIt IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(n)
`exempt as a securities financing transaction` MEANS
        periodIsRunning
    AND isASecuritiesFinancingTransaction
    AND ofATypeFinancedInTheTriPartyMarketInThatWeek
    AND markedToMarketDailyAndAtLeastAsOverCollateralized
    AND aggregateRiskProfileNoGreater
    AND topTierHoldingCompanyGuarantees
    AND notInformedByTheBoardItMayNotUseIt

-- (o): "Purchases of asset-backed commercial paper from an affiliated SEC-registered open-end investment company that holds itself
-- out as a money market mutual fund under SEC Rule 2a-7 ..., if the member bank: (1) Purchases the asset-backed commercial paper
-- on or after September 19, 2008; (2) Pledges the asset-backed commercial paper to a Federal Reserve Bank to secure financing from
-- the asset-backed commercial paper lending facility (AMLF) established by the Board on September 19, 2008; and (3) Has not been
-- specifically informed by the Board ... that the member bank may not use this exemption."
GIVEN
    fromAnAffiliatedMoneyMarketFund IS A BOOLEAN
    boughtOnOrAfterSeptember19Of2008 IS A BOOLEAN
    pledgedToAFederalReserveBankForAmlfFinancing IS A BOOLEAN
    notInformedByTheBoardItMayNotUseIt IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.42(o)
`exempt as a purchase of asset-backed commercial paper` MEANS
        fromAnAffiliatedMoneyMarketFund
    AND boughtOnOrAfterSeptember19Of2008
    AND pledgedToAFederalReserveBankForAmlfFinancing
    AND notInformedByTheBoardItMayNotUseIt
